ly pushed out and  we only ever really saw him in one more  episode after that I would have loved to  have seen him play more of a reoccurring  role but I do believe that the actor  Corey nemec actually had some other  things going on and he eventually went  on to do some other shows after Stargate  so for him it probably wasn't too much  of a big deal but as as a viewer  watching it I fell in love with Jonas  Quinn and when he left I was actually  quite sad although I was very thankful  at the same time because Daniel Jackson  was fantastic I would have liked to see  Jonas Quinn a little bit more but why  did Michael Shanks leave in the first  place  well according to reports essentially  Michael Shanks didn't really feel like  Daniel Jackson the character was being  pushed to his limits he wasn't being  utilized as well as he maybe could have  been and he felt that the character was  kind of stagnating he wasn't moving on  with characters like tilk we we see the  story arc and we see their characters  evolve tilk was essentially a slave he  was first branch of office and he led  the Jafar rebellion and eventually  created the fridge of our nation so we  saw that Arc play out over the course of  10 seasons with Michael Shanks with  Daniel Jackson his story arc kind of  came to a close his initial story arc  was that he wanted to find his wife  charay the woman that he met and married  on abidos who was taken as a host by  amunet his entire Mission his entire  core purpose was to find and free and  hopefully live a life again with Charo  now ultimately that didn't happen Chari  and amuna and up being killed by tilk  and after that it kind of made Daniel  Jackson's story arc irrelevant it was  over it was done  that was until the harshis's child  storyline came in which was the child  born from apophisina munet which is the  genetic offspring of those two human  hosts but with the knowledge of all the  goal that came before it they had the  genetic memory now that played out  up until about season four when we saw  the the really we saw the final  incarnation of that in ultimate power  and I think it's this reason that  Michael Shanks decided that his  storyline was done and he wasn't being  pushed as far as he could have been now  there are many reports basically saying  that Michael Shanks didn't like how the  writers were writing his character and  basically didn't like the style that  they were going with him but he has come  out and said that that wasn't true so I  don't think that for any minute Michael  Shanks had any ill intentions towards  the people who were writing his  character or to anyone like Brad Wright  or anything like that but he ultimately  decided to leave the show and in season  five when he ascended he had for all  intents and purposes left he did appear  a few times in season six and right at  the end of season six he returned fully  but in that in between stage he wasn't  part of the show going back to what I  mentioned about Jonas Quinn basically  replacing Daniel Jackson and having  Daniel Jackson Leave the show a lot of  fans were understandably quite angry  quite annoyed that Daniel Jackson had  died and they were very vocal about it  Michael Shanks has been reported as  saying that he didn't realize how  how important the character of Daniel  Jackson was to the people who enjoy  Stargate and it's one of them things  isn't it you don't understand your true  worth until people start telling you for  me Daniel Jackson has always been  heart of Stargate when Stargate returns  because I honestly believe it will if  he's not in it in any way it's not going  to be Stargate as we know it because he  is the heart and soul as I've just said  he's the heart and soul he is the  basically the reason why the Stargate  project even got a green lit in the  first place back in the 1994 movie he is  the one who deciphered the symbols and  basically figured out the address to  aberdos which is which led them to go to  aberdos defeat ra and that's where he  met his wife and that's what created his  initial story arc in the first four  seasons also but beyond that Beyond  actually helping to found the Stargate  program  he was also the voice of reason for many  people he wasn't part of the military he  was a civilian so therefore he could  basically say whatever he wanted and he  always thought with his heart the  character of Daniel Jackson really just  wanted to discover new things he yearned  for knowledge he wanted to figure out  ancient languages and he really wanted  to help people in other cultures he was  a humanitarian of sorts and for me I  think Daniel Jackson was that that kind  of character that the audience latches  on to the one that we can relate to  because he is a civilian just going  along for the ride for all intents and  purposes  he is the one that we we feel the most  for we want to see him succeed we want  to see what happens with we want to see  what happens with the rest of the team  of course we do but Daniel Jackson was  that vehicle for the audience and when  he left it kind of made it a little bit  like that vehicle had gone and Jonah  Jonas Quinn was a fantastic replacement  I've said before he was a fantastic  character I absolutely loved him but  because we we were so used to Daniel  Jackson  for the first four or five seasons  having him not be there for season six  it was a bit of an adjustment and the  audience didn't really adjust  as great as Jonas Quinn was we wanted  Daniel Jackson back and thankfully the  writers and Michael Shanks got together  and they basically wrote him back into  the show by by descending him back down  to the human plane of existence and  honestly it's one of those things  where we got more out of it than what we  what what we thought basically Michael  shanks's character Daniel Jackson's  character rather went on to do better  and better things he became more more  vital to the to the to the team it was  much more 